# Odd cyclic subgroups determined by the Vélu quotient's j

Theorem statement: `WeierstrassCurve.zmultiples_eq_of_veluQuotient_j_eq_of_transcendental`
(`15e5edb3-b3ba-566c-a842-036261074c96`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `4f9294dd-b7f9-5556-ad59-3851a2ac7a1b`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Work over the field $K = \mathrm{HahnSeries}\ \mathbb{Q}\ \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of Hahn series with
rational exponents and coefficients in an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $W$ be a
Weierstrass curve over $K$ whose discriminant is a unit (`W.IsElliptic`), and assume its
$j$-invariant $j(W)$ is transcendental over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $n$ be a natural number and let $Q,
Q'$ be points of the associated affine curve $W$ each of additive order exactly $2n+1$. For a point
$P$ write $\mathrm{coordsOrZero}(P)$ for its pair of affine coordinates, with the point at infinity
sent to $(0,0)$, and let $S_Q = \{\mathrm{coordsOrZero}(kQ) : 1 \le k \le n\} \subseteq K \times K$,
and similarly $S_{Q'}$; the Vélu quotient $\mathrm{veluQuotient}\ S$ is the Weierstrass curve with
the same $a_1, a_2, a_3$ as $W$ and with $a_4$ replaced by $a_4 - 5\sum_{P \in S} t(P)$ and $a_6$ by
$a_6 - b_2\sum_{P \in S} t(P) - 7\sum_{P \in S} w(P)$. Assume the discriminants of the two Vélu
quotients $\mathrm{veluQuotient}\ S_Q$ and $\mathrm{veluQuotient}\ S_{Q'}$ are nonzero — so that
both are elliptic and have a $j$-invariant — and that these two $j$-invariants are equal. Then the
cyclic subgroups generated by $Q$ and by $Q'$ coincide: $\mathbb{Z}Q = \mathbb{Z}Q'$ inside the
group of points of $W$.

This is the injectivity of $C \mapsto j(E/C)$ on cyclic subgroups of a fixed odd order $N = 2n+1$,
for a curve whose $j$-invariant is transcendental over $\mathbb{Q}$ (so that the curve has no extra
endomorphisms). It is used in the study of the modular polynomial $\Phi_N$ over the Hahn series
field: the fibre-polynomial factorisation into Vélu quotient $j$-invariants, the root-membership
criterion for odd level, and the construction of elliptic points with prescribed cyclic subgroup
orbits.

